From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:44:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Spell out the leading null group offset the offset pruning returns

OffsetPruningResult gains a third member, leading_null_group_offset,
and two returns in RowGroupReorderer still brace-initialize the first
two, so -Wmissing-field-initializers reports them. Upstream later
writes the zero out; this is that text.

Carried here until the engine brings the same change.

---
 src/duckdb/src/storage/table/row_group_reorderer.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/storage/table/row_group_reorderer.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/storage/table/row_group_reorderer.cpp
index 314848d596..9ba0ab6fb4 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/storage/table/row_group_reorderer.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/storage/table/row_group_reorderer.cpp
@@ -175,7 +175,7 @@ OffsetPruningResult FindOffsetPrunableChunks(It it, End end, const OrderByStatis
 			if (pruned_stats->CanHaveNull()) {
 				// Offset pruning can only remove a contiguous prefix of row groups. Once the first unresolved
 				// row group might still contribute NULLs to the ordered prefix, we cannot prune past it.
-				return {new_row_offset, pruned_row_group_count};
+				return {new_row_offset, pruned_row_group_count, 0};
 			}
 			// This row group has exactly row_group.count valid values. We can exclude those.
 			pruned_row_group_count++;
@@ -194,7 +194,7 @@ OffsetPruningResult FindOffsetPrunableChunks(It it, End end, const OrderByStatis
 		}
 	}
 
-	return {new_row_offset, pruned_row_group_count};
+	return {new_row_offset, pruned_row_group_count, 0};
 }
 
 } // namespace
